# Behaviors

## Framework semantics

Behaviors attach reusable find/save/delete lifecycle capabilities to Tables (Timestamp, Tree, Translate, soft-delete style packs). They are CakePHP’s mixin extension point for ORM concerns — not a dumping ground for HTTP or one-Table query helpers.

## Required behavior

- Prefer a Behavior when the capability must apply across multiple Tables with shared callbacks/finders/config.
- Prefer a custom finder on one Table when the concern is domain query semantics for that model only.
- Keep Behaviors focused on one coherent theme; split unrelated concerns.
- Check for an installed plugin Behavior before inventing a parallel one.

## Anti-patterns

- god-behavior
- Using a Behavior for single-Table query semantics that belong in a finder
- Free-floating services that reimplement Behavior lifecycle hooks

## Review checklist

- [ ] Cross-table lifecycle reuse → Behavior; one-Table query → finder
- [ ] Behavior theme is coherent (not a mixin junk drawer)
- [ ] No HTTP/authz logic inside Behaviors by default
